1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Cricket Scouting App — Coach Walkthrough

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:11,300
Three things today: tryout evaluations, team formation, and in-game tracking.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,600
SECTION 1 — FOR COACHES

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,900
Players are grouped into batches.

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:24,200
Each batch shows its player count right in the dropdown.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,500
Switching batches instantly filters the board.

7
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,800
Every player is evaluated against a skill rubric.

8
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:38,100
Skills are grouped into lettered sections — A, B, C...

9
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:43,400
Each skill is rated 1–5 stars, weighted by importance.

10
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:47,700
You can leave a note on any skill.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Fitness Assessment covers Yo-Yo, jump tests, and plank holds.

12
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,300
Save Evaluation locks it in.

13
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:00,600
Yo-Yo scores are color-coded automatically.

14
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:06,900
Green = 15.5+, Amber = 15.2–15.49, Red = below 15.2.

15
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:13,200
Shows up on the board, the player card, and here.

16
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,500
The card also shows self-declared profile and batting/bowling stats.

17
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:23,800
Two tabs: My Evaluation, and All Coaches.

18
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:30,100
Every coach rates independently — compare scores side by side.

19
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,400
Reports roll all of this up.

20
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:39,700
My Evals, Skill Notes, All Fitness Scores, Selection — one place for every view.

21
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
SECTION 2 — CREATING A TEAM PACKAGE

22
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:48,300
Each team gets 13 required slots, plus up to 3 reserves.

23
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:53,600
Assign players, then mark a Captain, Vice-Captain, and Wicketkeeper.

24
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:59,900
Admins can also mark a player Selected or Not Selected from their card.

25
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:04,200
That drives the Selected Players report.

26
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,500
Once finalized, an admin approves the package as the official roster.

27
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:13,800
SECTION 3 — IN-GAME RATINGS & OPPORTUNITY METRICS

28
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:18,100
Pick a team and a game number.

29
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:22,400
Rate any player on that roster.

30
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:28,700
Same rubric as tryouts — Batting, Bowling, Wicketkeeping, Fielding — scoped to one game.

31
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Checkboxes mark whether they actually batted or bowled that game.

32
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:40,300
Catches Dropped tracking and notes on every section, plus an Overall section.

33
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:46,600
Reopening Rate loads your last entry — it updates, it doesn't duplicate.

34
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:52,900
The Opportunity Sheet tracks batting order, bowling order, overs, and who coached.

35
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:58,200
View mode shows every game for a team side by side.

36
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:03,500
One glance tells you if playing time is rotating fairly.

37
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,800
That's the coach-facing app: evaluate, select, track.

38
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:13,100
Admin tools — approvals, settings — coming in a separate walkthrough.
